# Conventional Commits

When creating a git commit, the message MUST follow [Conventional Commits 1.0.0](https://www.conventionalcommits.org/en/v1.0.0/#specification).

```
<type>[optional scope][optional !]: <description>

[optional body]

[optional footer(s)]
```

- Type, OPTIONAL scope, OPTIONAL `!`, then REQUIRED `: ` and description.
- Description: imperative, concise, English (this repo's commit language).
- Body (OPTIONAL): one blank line after the description; free-form paragraphs.
- Footers (OPTIONAL): one blank line after the body; `Token: value` or `Token #value`. Tokens use `-` instead of spaces. `BREAKING CHANGE` (or `BREAKING-CHANGE`) is the exception and MUST be uppercase.

## Types

| Type | When |
| --- | --- |
| `feat` | New user-facing capability (MINOR) |
| `fix` | Bug fix (PATCH) |
| `docs` | Documentation only |
| `style` | Formatting; no behavior change |
| `refactor` | Restructure; no feat or fix |
| `perf` | Performance |
| `test` | Tests only |
| `build` | Cargo/workspace/deps |
| `ci` | CI |
| `chore` | Maintenance that is none of the above |

Prefer one type per commit. Split mixed work into multiple commits when possible.

## Scope

OPTIONAL noun in parentheses. In this workspace use a crate or `workspace`:

`feat(lull-spec):`, `fix(lull-protocol):`, `feat(lull-derive):`, `feat(lull-engine):`, `build(workspace):`

## Breaking changes

MUST be marked with `!` before `:` and/or a footer:

```
feat(lull-spec)!: rename Engine::step to process

BREAKING CHANGE: `Engine::step` is now `Engine::process`.
```

`!` in the prefix is enough; if `!` is used, a `BREAKING CHANGE:` footer MAY be omitted and the description SHALL describe the break.

## Examples

```
feat(lull-engine): add EchoEngine
fix(lull-protocol): reject trailing bytes after a frame
docs: document crate layout in README
build(workspace): share crate versions via workspace.dependencies
```
